    <p class="eyebrow">Red River Gorge Hiker</p>
    <h1>About Ryan D. Lewis</h1>
    <p class="lede">Ryan D. Lewis is an explorer and photographer whose work is centered on Kentucky’s Red River Gorge and Clifty Wilderness. Red River Gorge Hiker grew from the time he spends hiking, backpacking, camping, leading friends, searching for remote features, and returning to the landscape in changing seasons.</p>

    <p>Ryan’s photographs are connected to experience rather than collected as isolated views. A rainbow appeared while he was preparing for a Sheltowee Trace thru-hike he later completed. A winter arch required careful travel through severe ice and snow. A different campsite revealed an unexpected sunrise vantage. Remote waterfall exploration led to the discovery, measurement, documentation, and naming of Splatter Falls.</p>

    <p>The goal is to present both the image and the truth of how it was made. Each page uses verified capture information and Ryan’s own account of the day. Unknown facts remain unknown rather than being filled with invented detail.</p>

    <p>Ryan retains personal copyright ownership of every photograph. Red River Gorge Hiker is the public brand through which the work, stories, displays, prints, and selected puzzle products are presented.</p>

    <h2>The first collection is a beginning</h2>
    <p>The first collection is only a beginning. Future work may explore additional overlooks, contemplative places, winter scenes, waterfalls, arches, and the quieter experiences that develop through repeated time in the Gorge.</p>
